abstract: >-
  A scientific open-source research framework for short-term hourly rainfall prediction using
  a Two-Stage Hurdle Transfer Learning architecture. The system integrates macro-scale atmospheric
  reanalysis (Copernicus ERA5) and satellite precipitation observations (JAXA GSMaP NRT and NASA GPM IMERG)
  with micro-scale ground truth telemetry from an automated AWS IoT weather station (Jerukagung, Kebumen,
  Central Java, Indonesia). The modeling pipeline features two complementary paradigms: an Optuna-optimized
  Tree-based XGBoost model and a 24-hour diurnal-lookback BiDirectional LSTM deep learning network,
  calibrated via isotonic regression and evaluated across comprehensive classification, regression,
  and cumulative water-balance metrics.
